{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>From its two ends.</b> Perhaps it intends to say that he did not make the cover evenly, hammering with a mallet across the entire width of the cover and so forth, but rather at the time of melting he melted in a broad area the measure of the cover, and at its two ends he lavished gold in the amount that would suffice for the cherubim. And by this the verse's saying <b>from its two ends</b> is precisely understood."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:04.492379219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}